---
import DocumentLayout from "../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro";
import {
  contactEmail,
  issuesURL,
  threatModelURL,
} from "../data/site";
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="Support — Sealbreak"
  description="Get help with Sealbreak, the iPhone app for unsealing OpenBao and HashiCorp Vault with Face ID. Contact, requirements, and frequently asked questions."
  eyebrow="SUPPORT"
  heading="Help with Sealbreak."
>
  <p slot="lead">
    Questions, bug reports, and feedback are welcome. Never include an unseal
    share, root token, or other secret in a message or issue.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Email:</strong>{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Bugs and feature requests:</strong>{" "}
      <a href={issuesURL}>GitHub Issues</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      An OpenBao server, or a compatible HashiCorp Vault server, that uses a
      Shamir seal.
    </li>
    <li>
      An HTTPS endpoint for that server with a certificate your iPhone trusts.
    </li>
    <li>An iPhone with Face ID and a device passcode set.</li>
    <li>iOS 26 or later.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

  <h3>Where is my unseal share stored?</h3>
  <p>
    In the iOS Keychain on your iPhone. It is bound to that device, is not
    synced to iCloud, and is released only after Face ID. It never leaves the
    device except when Sealbreak sends it to the server you configured.
  </p>

  <h3>Can I export my share or move it to a new iPhone?</h3>
  <p>
    No. There is no export by design. On a new iPhone, import the share again
    from your own recovery copy.
  </p>

  <h3>What happens if I lose my iPhone?</h3>
  <p>
    The share on that iPhone may become unusable. The same can happen after
    Face ID changes, a device reset, or deleting the app. Sealbreak is not a
    backup. Always keep an independent recovery copy of every unseal share and
    a separate way to unseal your server.
  </p>

  <h3>Does Sealbreak send my share anywhere else?</h3>
  <p>
    No. Sealbreak connects directly to your server over HTTPS. There is no
    Sealbreak relay, and the app collects no data. See the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and the{" "}
    <a href={threatModelURL}>threat model</a> for details.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
